compute these Q values.

101
00:06:15,700 --> 00:06:17,940
But here, if we're going to
start thinking about just

102
00:06:17,940 --> 00:06:20,950
learning this from data
and from direct experience,

103
00:06:20,950 --> 00:06:22,673
that if we have a
deterministic policy,

104
00:06:22,673 --> 00:06:24,090
it's not going to
give us any data

105
00:06:24,090 --> 00:06:27,450
about trying different
actions in the same state.

106
00:06:27,450 --> 00:06:30,270
And so that's going to introduce
some important challenges

107
00:06:30,270 --> 00:06:31,680
that we have to
tackle when we're

108
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:33,780
trying to get data
about the world

109
00:06:33,780 --> 00:06:36,280
in order to learn an
optimal Q-function.

110
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:42,820
Great.

111
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:44,220
So what we're going
to be doing today then

112
00:06:44,220 --> 00:06:46,500
is try to think about
building on what we learned

113
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:48,880
last time about
policy evaluation,

114
00:06:48,880 --> 00:06:51,250
where we're trying to learn
directly from experience,

115
00:06:51,250 --> 00:06:54,400
to be able to evaluate how good
a particular decision policy is.

116
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:55,860
How do we leverage
that information

117
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:57,850
to then actually learn
an optimal policy,

118
00:06:57,850 --> 00:07:00,180
to actually learn a
good decision, you know,

119
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:03,340
a good policy without having to
model of how the world works?

120
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:05,850
So we don't have access
to an explicit parametric

121
00:07:05,850 --> 00:07:08,880
representation of the dynamics
model or the reward model.

122
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:12,340
And then we're also going
to talk about value function

123
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:13,060
approximation.

124
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:16,830
And in particular, we're
going to talk about Q-learning

125
00:07:16,830 --> 00:07:20,730
with deep neural
networks, a.k.a.

126
00:07:20,730 --> 00:07:24,240
DQN, which led to this
really seminal result

127
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:28,110
in having machines that can
just play directly from vision

128
00:07:28,110 --> 00:07:30,583
to learn how to play
games like Atari.

129
00:07:30,583 --> 00:07:32,250
But I'll just pause
here in case anybody

130
00:07:32,250 --> 00:07:33,875
has any questions or
