258
00:13:00,710 --> 00:13:04,340
Or you wouldn't change
it, and in that case--

259
00:13:04,340 --> 00:13:07,010
or you would improve.

260
00:13:07,010 --> 00:13:09,410
But when we did that proof,
we assumed policy improvement

261
00:13:09,410 --> 00:13:12,150
using a deterministic policy.

262
00:13:12,150 --> 00:13:14,120
And it turns out the
same property holds

263
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:16,860
with epsilon greedy policies.

264
00:13:16,860 --> 00:13:19,990
So if your policy is always
like an epsilon greedy policy,

265
00:13:19,990 --> 00:13:22,750
you can also get this kind
of monotonic improvement.

266
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:27,690
So in particular,
and I'm not going

267
00:13:27,690 --> 00:13:31,030
