I'll leave it in just for time.

268
00:13:31,030 --> 00:13:33,660
But what this shows
here is imagine

269
00:13:33,660 --> 00:13:36,242
that you have a Q-function,
you have some policy pi i.

270
00:13:36,242 --> 00:13:38,700
And you have a Q-function,
which tells you the state action

271
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:41,220
value for that policy pi i.

272
00:13:41,220 --> 00:13:45,540
And pi is e-greedy, which
means some of the time,

273
00:13:45,540 --> 00:13:48,000
it acts greedily with
respect to that Q-function.

274
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:51,210
And some of the time, it
selects an action at random.

275
00:13:51,210 --> 00:13:55,050
So that's what it means to be
an e-greedy policy with respect

276
00:13:55,050 --> 00:13:57,690
to that Q. It's making
those decisions when

277
00:13:57,690 --> 00:14:01,020
it's being greedy with
respect to that Q-function.

278
00:14:01,020 --> 00:14:03,090
So what this says
is that pi i plus 1

279
00:14:03,090 --> 00:14:07,500
is a monotonic improvement,
so that V pi i plus 1

280
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:10,250
is greater than V pi i.

281
00:14:10,250 --> 00:14:11,940
And we can prove this here.

282
00:14:11,940 --> 00:14:14,030
So essentially, we're
trying to prove in this case

283
00:14:14,030 --> 00:14:17,120
